  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road Summer 2002 was held at seven venues on nine days, from Sapporo on 20 July to Fukuoka on 11 August 2002, five of them at Pokémon Festa 2002. As in the spring, the top three of each league won a No. 1, 2 or 3 Trainer card printed with their name, in a boy's or a girl's version, mailed to them in September 2002; it was the last year of named trophy cards. Points earned in the side events bought holofoil Crystal Energy, Boost Energy and Warp Energy, all drawn by Kai Ishikawa, as well as card sleeves or Imakuni?'s signature.",
